{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Adam.</b> And it does not say 'a man, a man, of the house of Israel,' so as to include the converts — and likewise (Leviticus 1:2) 'when any man of you offers' — for there is one law for the citizen and for the convert in the offerings as well. And the convert is included so that he not defile another, for tzara'at is among the diseases that spread from the sick person to the healthy one." "<b>And he shall be brought.</b> Willingly or unwillingly, for whoever sees in him one of these signs will compel him to come." "<b>Or to one of his sons, the priests.</b> The sense of 'Aharon' is the anointed priest serving under him, and the sense of 'one of his sons, the priests' is ordinary priests [hedyotot] who are found outside the Temple, like the priests of Anatot." "And the word <b>the priests</b> means they must not be among the disqualified ones." "And the word <b>se'et</b> is like (Deuteronomy 32:24) 'burning [sherefet]' and likewise (Ezekiel 44:30) 'and the offering [umasha'at] of dough,' and (1 Chronicles 13:7) 'and they carried them [vayisa'em].' It is plausible that it is so called because fire's nature is to rise upward." "<b>Sapachat.</b> From the root of (1 Samuel 20:29) 'let me attach myself [usfachteni]' and (Isaiah 14:1) 'and they shall be joined [venispechu]' to the house of Ya'akov — a disease that gathers together into one place." "<b>Baheret.</b> From the root of 'bright [barir]' which is in the clouds, and it is known that it forms in the shape of a mark and a sign."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:50.310405732Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}